<title>INDIA: India L&amp;T expects financial closure on power plant.</title>
<headline>India L&amp;T expects financial closure on power plant.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian engineering and construction firm Larsen and Toubro Ltd (L&amp;T) said it expects to complete financing needs of its Bhilai power plant in the next three or four months.</p>
<p>&quot;Financial closure of the BhiLai Power Plant should be in three or four months' time,&quot; L&amp;T managing director Sudhakar Kulkarni told Reuters in an interview on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The plant has now made considerable progress,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>The Bhilai Power Supply Co Ltd, which is building the 500 MW power plant, is being promoted by L&amp;T jointly with the US-based Community Energy Alternatives and the Steel Authority of India Ltd (SAIL).</p>
<p>State-run SAIL, India's largest steel-maker, and L&amp;T will use the generated power.</p>
<p>-- Clarence Fernandez, Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
